    "observations": [
      "Assignment identity skips all actual-header access; after resize use current source test and destination-count/source-data/destination-data order.",
      "Concat initial copy reads count/output-data/left-data. Append captures right length and old output length, then uses current data after resize; raw memmove supports backward overlap.",
      "Prefix construction precedes caller cleanup. Concat failure cleans its own output; prefix caller cleans only the temporary. After success, capture temporary.data before output ownership and prefix disarm.",
      "Normal prefix getter/return uses captured data and current length+1 without clearing the temporary header. Failure there destroys output once and never retries prefix return.",
      "One real owned backing allocation supports borrowed overlapping assignment headers; they do not add separate pool returns.",
      "Compiler moves concat pointer comparison after output clears and EH state write before right-length load. Captured-pointer/ordinary C++ behavior is preserved; hardware-fault and private-frame timing are excluded."
    ]
